            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "In redfish naming conventions, these should just be \"bios1\" and \"bios2\".  No need to include some internal identifier the user doesn't care about."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/collection.hpp",
                    "line": 97,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Unique leaves has been a requirement of Redfish bmcweb collections since forever.  The problem this patch has overall is that now the rest APIs aren't generated consistently\n\n/xyz/openbmc_project/my_id -> turns into my_id\n\nbut now if another path gets added, suddenly that resource (that's supposed to be the same) changes to openbmc_project/my_id, which isn't how Redfish is supposed to work (see tree stability in the spec).\n\nI understand dbus and Redfish are in conflict here.  If you wanted to have a mode where we just expose the entire path (xyz_openbmc_project_my_id) and add it as a compile mode, that might work, but we shouldn't be changing resource URIs at runtime."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/collection.hpp",
                    "line": 100,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is the word \"software\" special here?"
                }
            ],
